Others have replied in depth, this is what I'd do differently:

Plan
1) dragon scale mail
2) enchant any ascension-kit armor you already have,
3) cursed genocides, Luck if necessary, polyself stuff, magic fountain
quaffing,
4) Castle, Valley
5) alchemy, wishing, remaining preparations
6) quest end level
7) Gehennom

> Should I use my (probable) wish from the blessed magic lamp or wait
> longer to see if I will need it?  If so, on what?
I'd definitely keep at least one permanent light source. I'd even wish
for one if that were possible in vanilla.

> Should I spend my scrolls of enchant weapon/armor, magic marker etc.
> or wait until I get better stuff?
I'd acquire MR, MC3, reflection, and then enchant up the armor I
intend to ascend with. In this case, probably the robe and the jumping
boots.

> What should I genocide?
I usually curse all genocides. In this case: silver dragon scale mail
unless you get reflection from another source, perhaps also gray
scales. Tengu in Sokoban - each scroll as 60.2% probability of giving
you telecontrol. Become a purple worm to get around corpse leaving
odds.
Keep a blessed genocide as escape item.

Don't genocide liches until you have a Gehennom strategy. As a
fallback, you can always levelport to the bottom and chase one up the
stairs, level for level.

> Since I have polycontrol and polymorph should I try to eat rings or
> something crazy like that?

Optionally, eat duplicate rings and amulets.

Lay some cockatrice eggs, too. If you feel like it, let a dozen or so
hatch for a supply of c-corpses.

You have a magic whistle. If you have the patience to grow up baby
dragons, lay eggs for silver/gray scale mail. If you're male, you may
have to feel like a new human a few times.

In order of preference, I'd acquire dragon scale mail from
1) cursed genocide,
2) confused throne looting (castle),
3) growing up baby dragons.
Wishes have better uses. Use Elbereth to keep dragons in melee range
so they can't use their breath attack.

> Magic trap dancing and then succubus wrasslin'?
I prefer magic fountain hunting, then alchimized gain ability. Before
you quaff from each fountain, put your entire open inventory (except
worn armor) into a sack to protect it from curses. Cursed "good" armor
doesn't harm you at all, you might as well uncurse it in the very end.
You might find you don't need foocubi anymore after this procedure.

> coaligned minetown temple
In case you want to farm, this is the place to do it. Let the priest
live for the sanctuary. Use the Sokoban scrolls of earth to make sure
he won't get in your way.
http://groups.google.com/group/rec.games.roguelike.nethack/browse_thread/thread/bb2908af1355815f/6b171b7823ef7245?lnk=gst&q=priest#6b171b7823ef7245

> castle on 25 (ran away as soon as I saw it, farthest I've gotten)
Since you have a ring of levitation, I'd grab a cockatrice corpse and
do the castle as soon as you have reflection and better armor. A
corpse lasts 220-260 turns. Use a wand (Elbereth) to protect yourself
against the touch of death from liches.

Another possibility is blessed object detection, then walk to the wand
as a levitating xorn, and wish up a magic resistance item (artifact)
before killing the soldiers.

> Armor
> uncursed +0 elven shield
> uncursed +0 elven boots
> blessed +4 crystal plate mail
> elven leather helm, +1 yugake

Better armor is your top priority. Use that magic marker to enchant up
silver/gray DSM, the robe, jumping boots, and the elven helm. You can
always wish for another marker.

> Scrolls
> lots!
If you find a wand of polymorph, polypiling blessed, #name-separated
blank scrolls in piles of four might be worth it. You especially want
enchant armor, genocide, and gold detection (for the Endgame).

> blessed scroll of enchant weapon
> 2 uncursed enchant weapon
Get +7 weapons.

> 4 uncursed create monster
> 2 uncursed genocide
> 4 uncursed tp
> 3 blessed TP
All of these belong cursed.

> 2 blessed remove curse
> 4 uncursed remove curse
If you don't yet have it, make unholy water. Bless the remaining
scrolls. Drop one on your main stash in case you get a cursed two-
hander and can't pray.

> 2 uncursed earth
for quest nemesis, mine town priest, possibly castle, escape item

Potions: collect some more foo-healing, speed, and gain energy. Make
gain ability/ full healing after fountain quaffing, before entering
Gehennom.

> Wands
> tele
> 4digging
> 2fire
Keep an identified, charged one of each in your inventory as escape
item.


